  "summary_en": "SDAIA's May 2025 guidelines for Saudi government employees using generative AI with government data. They apply the SDAIA AI Ethics Principles (fairness, reliability, transparency, privacy, accountability), require human review of outputs, bar use in critical decisions, and include a checklist and use-case examples. No robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Government entities must follow SDAIA AI Ethics Principles across the GenAI tool life cycle",
   "GenAI must not be used in critical decisions affecting individuals or vital national interests",
   "All GenAI outputs must be human-reviewed for accuracy, bias and harm",
   "Users must disclose AI-generated content to beneficiaries and offer non-automated channels",
   "Entities must train staff, restrict use to authorized personnel and keep usage records"
  ],
